    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25912" root="ضفر" body-key="D">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضَفِرٌ</span></b>  and [its n. un.] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضَفِرَةٌ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضَفْرٌ</span>. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كِنَانَةٌ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضَفِرَةٌ</span> [in the TA <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضفيرة</span>, evidently a mistranscription,] <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُمْتَلِئَةٌ</span> [i. e. <i>A full quiver</i>]. (S, O.
[Freytag writes <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كِنانةُ ضَفِرَةٌ</span>, and explains it as
meaning “ Gens Cinanah impleta est: ” but in
my copies of the S and in the O, it is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كِنَانَةٌ</span>.])

